1785291852877922	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.create	bn-3ly0	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPhase B turns the dossier spikes into a real semantic engine and real-code loop. The test strategy in docs/19 requires generated tiny systems, metamorphic relations, mutation campaigns, retained replay, differential oracles, and adversarial untrusted-input fuzzing. Those obligations must have explicit owners instead of being inferred from feature PR acceptance text.\n\n# Scope\nChild bones establish the semantic oracle, metamorphic suite, differential-disagreement policy, retained crashpack/mutation matrix, and resource-limited untrusted-artifact security suite. The harness starts with the reference engine, CIR, packs, and replicated register, and becomes the extension point for later optimized engines.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every docs/19 testing layer has an executable Phase B owner or an explicit later-phase owner.\n- [ ] A seeded semantic disagreement, replay regression, malformed artifact, and surviving mutant each fail closed and emit a minimized diagnostic fixture.\n- [ ] The Phase B real-code demonstration is retained as a permanent regression corpus.","kind":"goal","labels":["phase-b","quality","security"],"parent":"bn-3zt","size":"l","title":"Semantic differential, replay, and untrusted-input validation harness"}	blake3:N_CbKv3EFw6gJKbdXYqCIbL_02rU_05Wbt0U5f6akxQ
1785291890233670	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAg		item.update	bn-1bf	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPR 0 must turn seven load-bearing Revision 3 RFCs into normative, implementation-ready specifications before interface freeze. Each RFC has a distinct artifact/operation surface and can be reviewed independently, so this is a goal with one child per RFC rather than one seven-document leaf.\n\n# Shared Definition of Done\n- [ ] Every child defines field types, closed enums/lattices, versioning, RFC-2119 requirements, acceptance vectors, and failure behavior for its owned surface.\n- [ ] Each RFC is reconciled one-to-one with its plan section; disagreements are resolved in favor of an explicitly revised normative RFC.\n- [ ] Cross-RFC terminology, epochs, handles, budget dimensions, and error codes agree mechanically; dossier validation stays green."}	blake3:g01ctK8PIbAnY0ii-gqD7GLdaLEkGhEiIF7SRl_jW_8
1785291890243402	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAw		item.update	bn-1bf	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:U2tfc6UeHHdRX9ozuzdh4GIgkreIqL_5d4uMLfYEhTk
1785291890243688	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyBA		item.update	bn-1bf	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:GReQbUaJ-A1AG6OhtxIA5123MJ3GnMFQ6APf_A9kddI
1785291890256307	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyBQ		item.update	bn-1kq3	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nSD-09 specifies the continuumd operational contract; this goal implements its four independently testable storage and lifecycle responsibilities: purge/redaction and multi-user privacy, backup/verified restore, semantic-epoch migration, and engine-defect artifacts. The prior single leaf mixed separate failure domains and could not be owned or accepted incrementally.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every child has crash/fault injection and independently verifiable artifacts.\n- [ ] No operation silently rewrites, loses, or overstates previously published evidence.\n- [ ] The combined operational contract passes restart, disk-exhaustion, privacy, restore, migration, and defect-bundle drills."}	blake3:Bw8ptZTbhlaRkUlPVNaQmX86qhZvFhgCnlEk6CCvE0c
1785291890259294	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyBg		item.update	bn-1kq3	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:FW1wH58CgaBOZLudCGh9Uwo5doZ5M16MZc69Tf2xQR0
1785291890259610	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyBw		item.update	bn-1kq3	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:0Gm7Agruh_0eJ7tHDiclAkLQaq3i8zXPVGBgiL4cJHY
1785291890270224	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyCA		item.update	bn-13l	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nComplete corpus 1.0 after Waves 0-3 by porting Wave 4 and Wave 5 families at declared parity. Wave 4 spans materially different P2, P3, and P4 obligations, while Wave 5 is the integrated stress lane; child bones split those proof and implementation shapes so progress and blockers remain visible.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every Wave 4/5 family in validated-examples.csv reaches required_parity against the pinned upstream commit.\n- [ ] Oracle disagreements create minimized fixtures and block the affected claim.\n- [ ] Deterministic corpus CI and per-family interaction-artifact checks remain green."}	blake3:4yamVGpoWsGrWGi_y1Rt8F1pDzfkUafEE0RsKVf8FJE
1785291890273052	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyCQ		item.update	bn-13l	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:8AC2numxgSp817FgZbHFnkf9aUXRBj1RDML6JpaPhAM
1785291890273561	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyCg		item.update	bn-13l	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:pxZtqHqKF0TVHmH074t2tEVoUvt7Hm8KeoZ6aNkj4IA
1785291890285203	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyCw		item.update	bn-3ei	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nFirst real-system adoption program. The candidate is selected by the recruitment funnel, then proceeds through a measured baseline, model/instrumentation and correspondence, real repair plus workflow cutover, and independent acceptance/documentation. These are separately reviewable milestones rather than one externally paced leaf.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bespoke DST is removed and separate TLA+ is no longer required for normal development.\n- [ ] Agent-driven repair is used on a real reviewed change.\n- [ ] Assurance envelopes and operating cost are measured from retained evidence, with rollback criteria recorded."}	blake3:PBdzrkHL9L8sbMv_-39om91TNL3AlOFzaxIBTJPBpJI
1785291890288506	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyDA		item.update	bn-3ei	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:4S949d0eFHPaQDjnaYb2pHHZE61zXNRBmODHU1zrt7Q
1785291890288767	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyDQ		item.update	bn-3ei	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:bH1LZHz1v4yApvxTIpmKUPglj7UVgsuoNSJEs8gQdz4
1785291890299482	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyDg		item.update	bn-23a	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nSecond real-system adoption program, deliberately materially different from Migration A in domain and architecture. It repeats the same evidence-bearing stages so the two-system G10 result is comparable without treating either migration as one opaque leaf.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Material difference from Migration A is recorded before implementation begins.\n- [ ] Bespoke DST and routine separate TLA+ workflow are retired under explicit rollback criteria.\n- [ ] Real agent repair, assurance envelopes, operating cost, and independent acceptance are recorded."}	blake3:vSMlBQ_2bNm4QaBOB37IX7-DX0pc__c_PJmapp1O_AQ
1785291890302368	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyDw		item.update	bn-23a	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:G55HNmZUTpQKGaYaUgFQ1W7dnM0knmGf2cPnulmJrHA
1785291890302609	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyEA		item.update	bn-23a	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:6xd0K6sM267ZJuH78iyspMgD6biUKi6T6iuPgJ3HHz0
1785291890316634	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyEQ		item.update	bn-2dv	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase C caps 17 Wave 0/1 families at P2 because their temporal/refinement or theorem obligations require Phase D machinery. Split the raises into P3 and P4 child lanes so liveness/refinement and Lean theorem work can proceed and report independently.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All deferred P3 families meet temporal/refinement parity.\n- [ ] All deferred P4 families meet theorem parity with explicit axiom manifests and bridge theorems.\n- [ ] Corpus CI derives full required-parity status from per-family evidence."}	blake3:GVbnGjdphS-ZTtoszugR68ntg_yB2lWpp5vCBdX1EZ4
1785291890319733	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyEg		item.update	bn-2dv	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:QpJoxySnSvBz1IC-fbQAuklaZ8fRsKni4zeIXC5HUTU
1785291890320082	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyEw		item.update	bn-2dv	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:LZ6iRmyzr-t2PhOThakV6zZUYbOW7HuChC9OvyigjR0
1785291890331795	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyFA		item.update	bn-1qy	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nCorpus checkpoint 0.5 requires Waves 0-2 at required parity plus five named P5 implementation-refinement exemplars. P5 entails a real asupersync implementation, instrumentation coverage, deterministic replay, schedule/fault exploration, and independent proof evidence; each exemplar therefore has its own child bone plus a checkpoint audit.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] TV-023, TV-025, TV-028, TV-029, and TV-039 each satisfy P5 independently.\n- [ ] Waves 0-2 remain at required parity.\n- [ ] Checkpoint 0.5 is recorded against the pinned corpus commit only after the completeness audit passes."}	blake3:hURgfvE2Uth-ibgrNzt7ENqeS3xZoczomrl-YsQ1a38
1785291890334799	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyFQ		item.update	bn-1qy	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:gyIyHDOBra4EM4I1wmlIc7pxh6eGBG-DyE99eIpvHeA
1785291890335132	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyFg		item.update	bn-1qy	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:IYXsDSfymju5Es_NQT4Ut0DVy0zdhMi2zIfJxJsWW0M
1785291890346068	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyFw		item.update	bn-20jv	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase A establishes the implementation quality floor before later crates proliferate. Child bones separately own algebraic/property suites, persistent fuzz infrastructure, and concurrency/sanitizer validation. Phase B has a distinct semantic differential/replay goal, so this goal is the reusable CI substrate and Phase A critical-path coverage rather than a catch-all for future engines.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every Phase A canonical/wire input has property or fuzz coverage with seeded failure controls.\n- [ ] CAS publication and task lifecycle have deterministic concurrency tests plus sanitizer coverage.\n- [ ] Corpora and failures persist in CI and produce reproducible diagnostics."}	blake3:7qDjtLSnrHkshuRM9oTcRKuXp1n7F48Ewnom_QsWZZw
1785291890348968	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyGA		item.update	bn-20jv	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:l7ZRcMLybwCPIWvqA11ckmYcMqGxmg_55SvtO6jFFRM
1785291890349198	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyGQ		item.update	bn-20jv	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:HSy5LaZeukr3o6XRAyyKR5Jubzy7-RZ1zbV9geYe6bY
1785291890361639	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyGg		item.update	bn-281l	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nUser documentation is a release surface, not one writing task. Child bones own the generated CLI/API reference, human workflow tutorials, tokio onboarding and assurance guidance, and the migration/runbook path validated by Migration B.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Reference text is mechanically checked against shipped schemas and golden output.\n- [ ] Tutorials cover the three human docs/34 workflows and satisfy accessibility requirements.\n- [ ] Migration B follows the written guide; gaps become tracked documentation defects."}	blake3:9-112ZrozB4z_h1HuoAF5n4f_o2HgBE5qm9rX6XkPq0
1785291890364312	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyGw		item.update	bn-281l	{"field":"size","value":"l"}	blake3:jVbJnKr7eixRy2fRmM-BhxiVaI8v3P52puPXlhMgwgo
1785291890364643	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyHA		item.update	bn-281l	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:0-_hWWLmAFcQZmBywpwGnX774N64VDdTiY9jwxSUpno
1785291890376191	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyHQ		item.update	bn-1w93	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nG10 needs both documented assurance envelopes and evidence that operating cost is acceptable. These have different inputs and reviewers, so child bones own them separately while this goal combines their release verdict.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every shipped lane documents exactly what it can and cannot claim.\n- [ ] Both real migrations publish comparable compute, latency, storage, and maintenance cost evidence.\n- [ ] The G10 cost decision cites a predeclared acceptance policy rather than an after-the-fact judgment."}	blake3:F-1gbhVnqDb2yb1Z1wbpIQUW38D4IAyJJ7ELYvUzzJA
1785291890380714	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyHg		item.update	bn-1w93	{"field":"size","value":"m"}	blake3:LTca1HuwStGsqKg_YqeGFJmRmiXZbwKrv-GfM0pzZw0
1785291890381018	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyHw		item.update	bn-1w93	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:yHOnL_KD4duMEs-XQFuzb7suB2qobB7VzaVrwyUbf3k
1785292046890603	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyIA		item.create	bn-3ffu	{"description":"# Context\nComplete RFC 0026 as the normative daemon protocol specification, aligned with plan §§4 and 10 and the SD-01 IDL.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every operation has typed request, response, error, capability, pagination, idempotency, and version-window semantics.\n- [ ] Task budgets, continuations, evidence subscriptions, and N/N-1 negotiation agree with the normative IDL.\n- [ ] Golden wire vectors and malformed-input expectations are specified for both encodings.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","phase-a","protocol"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"m","title":"RFC 0026 — Normative continuumd native protocol specification"}	blake3:QJYLXAr082fydwIFbWwQPmBScDEIKkdDyLP_hRTqam0
1785292046963239	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyIQ		item.create	bn-26fh	{"description":"# Context\nMake RFC 0027 implementation-ready for bounded agent operations and least-authority handoff.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tool schemas, deterministic ordering, result bounds, capability delegation, expiry, and denial behavior are normative.\n- [ ] Privileged intent and promotion operations cannot be inferred from model output or handle possession.\n- [ ] Conformance examples cover single-agent, handoff, stale-handle, and prompt-injection cases.\n","kind":"task","labels":["aci","docs","phase-a","protocol","security"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"s","title":"RFC 0027 — Normative agent tool and capability protocol specification"}	blake3:RwYu55EQB7x3DJvg3vI2ZD9IH6EBRQgKu5j7_TD5AW4
1785292047033661	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyIg		item.create	bn-4xxw	{"description":"# Context\nSpecify Context Pack compilation, omission transparency, replay identity, and deterministic expansion as a machine contract.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Required fields, assurance envelope, budgets, omission manifest, expansion handles, and replay references are typed.\n- [ ] Truncation and unavailable/redacted expansion fail with explicit typed outcomes.\n- [ ] Acceptance vectors include invariant, reachability, and proof-target packs.\n","kind":"task","labels":["aci","docs","evidence","phase-a"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"s","title":"RFC 0028 — Normative Context Pack and expansion protocol specification"}	blake3:uTENO61_jLYGVvVYzLvujLDVpWWUZ19KUdvjUT9sS5w
1785292047104271	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyIw		item.create	bn-3hkk	{"description":"# Context\nComplete RFC 0030 for content-addressed queries, reuse-edge classes, invalidation explanations, and the Incremental Parity Audit.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exact, Validated, Conservative, and Experimental reuse have closed definitions and downgrade rules.\n- [ ] Sampling, mismatch minimization, class quarantine, crash safety, and proof/certificate freshness are normative.\n- [ ] Clean-versus-incremental conformance vectors cover every semantic query stage.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","incremental","phase-a"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"m","title":"RFC 0030 — Normative incremental query and parity-audit specification"}	blake3:jjSofrsRr6fAGolYXAnXBI-Zl_xmsHr_PBVMGlVFfng
1785292047174027	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyJA		item.create	bn-39my	{"description":"# Context\nDefine the typed diff classifications used to stop reward hacking and to calculate evidence impact.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All protected field groups have normalization, ordering where defined, Unknown behavior, and impact-set rules.\n- [ ] Property, assumption, bound, observer, fault, fairness, assurance, security, and abstraction-map cases are normative.\n- [ ] Unsupported fragments fail closed and cannot enter ordinary repair promotion.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","intent","phase-a","security"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"m","title":"RFC 0031 — Normative semantic and protected-intent diff specification"}	blake3:m8hXLA_bTHY3M-Iz3Lf7CA3UrC1-2xTBpEMT4W3jM_Q
1785292047245428	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyJQ		item.create	bn-3i38	{"description":"# Context\nSpecify the complete repair transaction, twelve promotion gates, phase profiles, cost governance, and independent receipt verification.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Begin, apply, evaluate, and promote state transitions are total and idempotent.\n- [ ] Phase B/C/D gate profiles and NotYetEnforced semantics are normative and never render absent evidence as passed.\n- [ ] Failure, budget exhaustion, rollback, and forged-reference cases have typed outcomes and test vectors.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","evidence","phase-a","repair"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"m","title":"RFC 0032 — Normative repair transaction and promotion receipt specification"}	blake3:AC3c4tRAuzODo4f28dVEWHyYbnN_ddbUaF1IvKKv0DE
1785292047320780	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyJg		item.create	bn-2s6q	{"description":"# Context\nComplete the Intent Contract schema, custody, signed-bundle convergence, acceptance-chain, locking, and revision procedure.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All fifteen protected field groups and closed policy verbs are typed and reconciled with the schema.\n- [ ] Canonical identity, three-way semantic merge, conflicts, signature verification, and evidence invalidation are normative.\n- [ ] Golden identity, policy, convergence, and adversarial mutation vectors are specified.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","intent","phase-a","security"],"parent":"bn-1bf","size":"m","title":"RFC 0037 — Normative Intent Contract registry and convergence specification"}	blake3:SSYRCa_kTKA4pu_9G5YxWsZYq65bqK3ORI9OfbJWebg
1785292047390854	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyJw		item.create	bn-3cft	{"description":"# Context\nImplement reachability GC, coverage summarization, encrypted sensitive artifacts, purge-by-key-shredding, typed Redacted stubs, and the cross-principal dedup policy.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Purged or summarized content remains commitment-verifiable and downgrades dependent claims explicitly.\n- [ ] Disk exhaustion and concurrent GC cannot truncate or half-publish an artifact.\n- [ ] Cross-user dedup is off by default and cannot serve as an existence oracle without explicit sharing policy.\n","kind":"task","labels":["kernel","phase-c","security"],"parent":"bn-1kq3","size":"m","title":"Artifact retention, purge, Redacted stubs, and multi-user dedup privacy"}	blake3:9dhpXw5M_P4PR_of8bGttAfHew35yfKhk1OayXZxaps
1785292047465149	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyKA		item.create	bn-1ufb	{"description":"# Context\nImplement backup and verified restore for CAS, evidence ledger, intent registry, and audit log.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Restore re-hashes content, runs the index verifier, and emits a signed restore report.\n- [ ] Missing referenced content becomes Redacted(lost, commitment), never a disappearing receipt.\n- [ ] Crash injection during backup and restore leaves a recoverable, deterministic state.\n","kind":"task","labels":["kernel","phase-c","quality"],"parent":"bn-1kq3","size":"m","title":"Backup manifests, verified restore, and append-only audit export"}	blake3:UQvv15pvMeSMSgCyfnh_lLejraE8GhmbxxhuqgTu5wM
1785292047534749	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyKQ		item.create	bn-1gn2	{"description":"# Context\nImplement semantic-epoch advance without mutating published artifacts.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every advance publishes Preserved, Revalidate, or Incompatible per artifact class plus estimated blast radius.\n- [ ] At most two epochs coexist; continuations remain pinned and fork rather than migrate in place.\n- [ ] Re-derived artifacts receive new identities and SUPERSEDES edges, with migration rollback tested.\n","kind":"task","labels":["incremental","kernel","phase-c"],"parent":"bn-1kq3","size":"m","title":"Two-epoch semantic migration and per-artifact compatibility reports"}	blake3:ePPuLDOi5gfJBbYvCdaXMv5uYHvoyBWRg8pt9FpPhhs
1785292047603535	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyKg		item.create	bn-3su4	{"description":"# Context\nMake parity mismatches, replay divergence, engine crashes, and explanation-validation failures first-class defect evidence.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each defect artifact pins all inputs, epochs, engine identity, and a minimized reproduction under redaction policy.\n- [ ] continuum doctor creates a shareable, independently verifiable bundle.\n- [ ] OpenTelemetry health data stays outside semantic evidence and cannot strengthen assurance.\n","kind":"task","labels":["evidence","kernel","phase-c","quality"],"parent":"bn-1kq3","size":"s","title":"Engine-defect artifacts, continuum doctor bundles, and telemetry separation"}	blake3:UZz3Vts212An81-lAzEI1c-bNIVTjofulFqB8MUq1SY
1785292047672048	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyKw		item.create	bn-29bf	{"description":"# Scope\nPort the Wave 4 families whose declared parity is P2, including symbolic puzzles, probability, security protocol, storage structure, filesystem, and Disruptor cases named in validated-examples.csv.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each pinned configuration has bounded semantic parity against its upstream oracle.\n- [ ] Unsupported symbolic or probabilistic features are explicit and do not count as passing.\n","kind":"task","labels":["corpus","phase-f"],"parent":"bn-13l","size":"m","title":"Wave 4 P2 behavioral ports: symbolic, probability, protocol, and storage cases"}	blake3:MbYtQY1cTCW1iRNVmNHlC2c5Qngt1NEWuMxw2mjy5fA
1785292047740300	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyLA		item.create	bn-2z63	{"description":"# Scope\nBring the Wave 4 P3 families, including Slush, Disk Paxos, Nano Blockchain, and DAG consensus, to temporal/refinement parity.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fairness, liveness, finite-prefix treatment, and refinement correspondence are explicit per family.\n- [ ] Intentionally failing temporal cases agree with the pinned oracle and produce inspectable fair-cycle evidence.\n","kind":"task","labels":["corpus","phase-f","proof"],"parent":"bn-13l","size":"m","title":"Wave 4 P3 temporal ports: consensus, durability, and blockchain cases"}	blake3:SJBSgjZ6TJrmAWgE_M_nuKLN6CzFH-tOZ4wPmK2th4g
1785292047810830	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyLQ		item.create	bn-2a7y	{"description":"# Scope\nBring the Wave 4 P4 families in validated-examples.csv to theorem parity, including bridge theorems over executable encodings.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each key theorem is checked in Lean with no sorry and with explicit axiom manifests.\n- [ ] The executable model-to-theorem bridge is independently checked and stale evidence invalidates fail closed.\n","kind":"task","labels":["corpus","phase-f","proof"],"parent":"bn-13l","size":"m","title":"Wave 4 P4 theorem ports: abstraction, storage, scheduling, and transactions"}	blake3:7pjbSkPo5QXjJTyMyhmbTiAS5FnX4J11slOAcYzSu_U
1785292047883181	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyLg		item.create	bn-1ium	{"description":"# Scope\nPort the four Wave 5 metacircular and industrial stress families at declared parity.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Large module closures, deep refinement, VIEW/ALIAS/CONSTRAINT behavior, symmetry, and industrial trace scale are exercised.\n- [ ] Performance evidence is compared at equal semantics and assurance with raw data retained.\n- [ ] Every disagreement is minimized and blocks only the affected claim class.\n","kind":"task","labels":["corpus","phase-f","quality"],"parent":"bn-13l","size":"l","title":"Wave 5 integrated stress ports: TLC, TCP, level checking, and German cache"}	blake3:tbEnYYwX0phdcqbqDcpHNtfiFcD3XtBuu90pnsBQqFc
1785292047950116	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyLw		item.create	bn-20jc	{"description":"# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Existing DST and TLA+ workflows, incidents, runtime costs, and unsupported areas are measured before intervention.\n- [ ] Protected target intent, success thresholds, data policy, cutover criteria, and rollback triggers are accepted by the system owner.\n","kind":"task","labels":["governance","phase-f"],"parent":"bn-3ei","size":"m","title":"Migration A baseline, target intent, and cutover/rollback contract"}	blake3:KWfE59h6LHUWLM8qjvT7p57NR6cg46PMR_x0si7c8u8
1785292048020310	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyMA		item.create	bn-31mx	{"description":"# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The target system has a native model and declared instrumentation/fidelity profile.\n- [ ] Concrete events map to model actions with uncovered effects failing closed.\n- [ ] Baseline incidents replay or are explicitly outside the accepted scope.\n","kind":"task","labels":["adapter","engine","phase-f"],"parent":"bn-3ei","size":"m","title":"Migration A model, instrumentation, and model-program correspondence"}	blake3:YfuIbme2G2HNqP5NjaCVTTV4RY6zDyHRxMtpml4v4CI
1785292048092081	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyMQ		item.create	bn-ahj9	{"description":"# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An agent diagnoses and repairs a real reviewed change under protected intent and promotion gates.\n- [ ] The team removes bespoke DST and no longer needs a separate TLA+ workflow for normal development.\n- [ ] Rollback remains possible until the predeclared observation window closes.\n","kind":"task","labels":["aci","governance","phase-f","repair"],"parent":"bn-3ei","size":"l","title":"Migration A real repair trial and DST/TLA+ workflow cutover"}	blake3:THd0th8SvRPCoCJ3Fh4nrLdeZJARHfe8AsbKsh89YsI
