1785292253374055	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2gE		item.update	bn-2ee	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase C exit / G5: the edit/check/explain loop must meet the docs/34 p50/p95 table, including failure-to-rendered-explanation, on the reference workload WHILE the deterministic saturating background workload generator (bn-1rxk) is active. This task owns instrumentation, workload manifests, statistical treatment, and the gate evidence; Phase F may rerun it under the full multi-agent workbench as hardening, but Phase C cannot defer the required measurement.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every docs/34 interaction row is measured reproducibly at p50/p95 with warm/cold distinctions and hardware manifest.\n- [ ] The bn-1rxk saturation profile is active for the gate run; foreground and background spend are reported separately.\n- [ ] Results and raw samples are published as evidence artifacts and regression-gated in CI."}	blake3:oasdNLDmAFT4j_vnSX2obXS7u5phXcx9N-y5lSf0BP4
1785292253401858	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2wE		item.update	bn-1s0	{"field":"title","value":"Four-role swarm orchestration and full-workbench load profiles"}	blake3:bCy78gnzG7aZId4RWrypnxNJvbNEghNdqjr5aqGSj74
1785292253409111	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3AE		item.update	bn-1s0	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nWorkbench slice: planner, repairer, prover, and reviewer coordinate over one workspace/intent with isolated handles and enforced capabilities. Phase C already owns the deterministic saturation generator required to close G5; this task reuses and extends those profiles with real role behavior for Phase F scale and cost evidence.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A four-role swarm completes a repair end to end without hidden session coupling.\n- [ ] Full-workbench load profiles reproduce the Phase C foreground/background accounting and expose orchestration overhead.\n- [ ] Stalled, duplicate, adversarial, and budget-exhausted roles terminate or suspend with typed evidence."}	blake3:K6HRjySlHzMhSBIAiOO3Ubvx3EPuOcSSQ8eKXNcLm_o
1785292253429104	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3QE		item.update	bn-iyk	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase F delivers concurrent agent swarms working one workspace under enforced authority. G0-DX-12 validated only an authority table; this goal implements linearized promotion, CAS status transitions, conflict materialization, isolated handles, four-role orchestration, and the full red-team campaign. The Phase C saturation generator already closed the G5 latency requirement; Phase F reuses it for hardening and operating-cost evidence.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Concurrent adversarial swarm cannot create an unauthorized intent edge or promote false evidence.\n- [ ] Conflicting proposals and status races materialize deterministically rather than losing updates.\n- [ ] Full-workbench load and red-team results are retained; fallback to a single-writer integrator is taken if enforcement cannot ratify."}	blake3:iF7TGra4T0cI8uc5k6tqwYSarWB6ra9jn5uyIqE_eL0
1785292253455116	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3gE		item.update	bn-waj3	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase C (G5, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52).\n\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] docs/34 p50/p95 table, including explain, is met on the reference workload WITH bn-1rxk saturating background load active.\n- [ ] Incremental Parity Audit matches clean builds; reuse classes quarantine correctly; Conservative-collapse remains healthy.\n- [ ] bn-d4fm shows zero reachability mismatch against the unreduced reference and certified claims fall back on mismatch.\n- [ ] bn-1p10 proves incremental cache/publication crash consistency and proof-freshness recovery.\n- [ ] Semantic artifacts are byte-identical across the docs/19 determinism matrix.\n- [ ] Evidence queries and context compilation meet docs/34 targets at at least 10^7 nodes.\n- [ ] bn-18pl passes the explicit-snapshot cross-surface edit/check/explain integration.\n- [ ] Gate criteria are permanent regressions; docs/52 and plan §22 G5 are reconciled in one commit."}	blake3:SNJbvbt9I66GhjWMJ8-_3Lb301GPvoMl61UW3Duzr1k
1785292253482403	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3wE		item.update	bn-1itt	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase B, based on evidence produced by bn-2a42 rather than inferred from separately green components.\n\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] bn-2a42 runs the plan §25 nine-step demonstration on a retained REAL asupersync failure under the Phase B gate profile.\n- [ ] The compact Context Pack preserves replay; the agent identifies ack-before-durability and proposes the semantic guard repair.\n- [ ] Intent is unchanged; exact replay, neighboring cancellation/crash schedules, property mutations, and known mutants pass.\n- [ ] Promotion receipt lists gates 9 and 10 as NotYetEnforced and independently verifies every reference.\n- [ ] Human review projection exposes the semantic diff, unknowns, cost, and decision.\n- [ ] The Phase B semantic validation goal is green; re-homed DX-04/DX-06 carry evidence.\n- [ ] Gate criteria are permanent regressions; docs/52 and plan §22 G3/G4 are reconciled."}	blake3:v4h4VjgVsX_udulrM4HyfG9I9HsOcbKKaoRd3LHUhSk
1785292253512240	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4AE		item.update	bn-3cpt	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase D (G6, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52). The integrated corpus claim is produced by bn-26bz.\n\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] bn-26bz carries one nontrivial corpus protocol through safety, liveness, real asupersync code, proof receipts, and independently verified refinement.\n- [ ] Lean foundations kernel-check with no placeholders; theorem/axiom manifests are complete; certificate mutations are rejected.\n- [ ] Proof requests are isolated/cancellable and agent proof repair is accepted only by the kernel.\n- [ ] Proof Context Packs measurably improve proof-worker success/cost.\n- [ ] Wave 0/1 P3/P4 raises and Waves 2/3 checkpoint 0.2 are complete as Phase D local deliverables.\n- [ ] Re-homed DX-08/DX-11 carry evidence; gate 9 enters the promotion profile; docs/52 and plan §22 are reconciled."}	blake3:N8NlM9aTigEeM35_kEkOuRFGhD0IzrKd3Wa-GuZZ1Pw
1785292253538426	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4QE		item.update	bn-o1oy	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase E (G7, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52). bn-26ij owns the integrated invention-to-materialization evidence; bn-268s owns corpus checkpoint 0.5.\n\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] bn-26ij demonstrates known-solution rediscovery and at least one behaviorally novel candidate under a declared envelope.\n- [ ] Semantic diversity, hidden-variant generalization, independent verification, and explicit unknown versus unrealizable behavior hold.\n- [ ] A promoted candidate materializes model, Rust/asupersync skeleton, proof obligations, and linked receipts.\n- [ ] Corpus checkpoint 0.5 passes for Waves 0-2 plus all five named P5 exemplars.\n- [ ] Re-homed DX-07 carries evidence; docs/48 preregistration is published before the Phase F study.\n- [ ] Gate criteria are permanent regressions; docs/52 and plan §22 G7 are reconciled."}	blake3:AiL584Zpzq6yg_U-f8Jy18sZ1hFuYtC-Rk9PBst7wis
