1785294221294930	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoQI		item.update	bn-2hm	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase A's designated opening PR (plan §21.1) — documentation and decisions, not code. The Revision 3 RFCs started as summaries; review 5 already absorbed large plan sections into RFCs 0026/0027/0030/0032/0037/0038, but full specification form (field types, enums, classification lattices, IDL, versioning, RFC-2119 language) and the remaining validator-tracked spec debt are this PR. Child tasks cover each open debt item (SD-01/07/08/09/10) and the program decisions.\n\n# Why this comes first\nInterface freeze is fail-closed: PR 5 (native protocol kernel) may not merge before PR 0 closes, so every wire-visible decision is settled on paper before any interface exists to ossify. Where plan prose and RFC disagree, the RFC is corrected and becomes NORMATIVE — the plan is a map, not the spec (plan §25).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria (START_HERE PR 0 exit)\n- [ ] RFCs 0026, 0027, 0028, 0030, 0031, 0032, 0037 are normative specifications (field types, enums, lattices, IDL, versioning, RFC-2119 language), each reconciled one-to-one with its plan section.\n- [ ] The pre-freeze open-debt set (plan §25, validator check_spec_debt) reads EMPTY in validation-results.json — not only the seven RFC expansions.\n- [ ] Product license decided (permissive, compatible with asupersync and solver adapters, §21.1).\n- [ ] Corpus per-family redistribution audit exists (required before any public benchmark release).\n- [ ] ADR-0029 rule recorded: foreign oracle tooling (TLC, Apalache, solvers) never ships in release binaries.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEvery fail-closed property later phases rely on (typed errors, epochs, authority splits, redaction) is specified here before code exists to violate it."}	blake3:AGu_rYEQbZRkbcWgH4UxBBhR1jCUeBhAScr15V3qKaQ
1785294221323715	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyogI		item.update	bn-2en	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase B's opening PR (plan §21.1): instrument asupersync's narrow primitives to emit canonical semantic events — the raw material for CIR, minimization, and the debugger. START_HERE PR 14.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nJournal task/region lifecycle; reserve/commit/abort; cancellation phases; obligations; virtual time; channel communication. One adapter crate; supported upstream window N and N−1 covered by the adapter conformance corpus in CI against upstream pre-releases; an upstream breaking release opens a scheduled adapter epoch (§4.6) visible in envelopes; explicit semantic-hook contract; the model core never depends on asupersync (dependency-island rule).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Identical controlled choice logs produce canonical identical semantic events.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEverything G4 promises (causal debugging of REAL code) starts from a trustworthy semantic journal; canonicality here is what makes replay exact."}	blake3:SgAE21hMUFr1B3F0hggQYl-fXHvWreCtW3oqZvEzj-k
1785294221351327	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyowI		item.update	bn-z2l	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase C's opening PR (plan §21.1): the §9 incremental semantic database, built or adopted per the PR 22a ADR (hard dep — PR 23 may not merge before PR 22a). START_HERE PR 23.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nContent-addressed queries for parsing, model construction, property automata, exploration, context, and diff. Classify reuse edges as Exact/Validated/Conservative/Experimental.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Property-only edit does not rebuild unrelated extraction.\n- [ ] Model action edit invalidates the reachable graph and dependent context (invalidation cone matches declared dependency classes).\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nInteractive latency (G5, docs/34 table) is impossible without trustworthy reuse; the four edge classes are how reuse stays honest (mismatches quarantine the CLASS, not the world — plan §9.5)."}	blake3:jqMa-Nb1Y-fpB18LDVrRX2Cjh0ruA7Tt36ENlUubVsA
1785294221378084	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypAI		item.update	bn-lb8	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase D's opening PR (plan §21.1): the proof SERVICE over the environment pinned in PR 4a. Closes re-homed G0-DX-11 (proof-service isolation: concurrent Lean epochs, malicious inputs, cancellation → deterministic isolated results and resource bounds). START_HERE PR 28.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nPer-request isolation and cancellation; goals; diagnostics; receipts with theorem/axiom manifests; relevant-context extraction consuming the Phase C proof-pack format. (Lean pinning and T0/T1 are PR 4a, NOT here.)\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Concurrent requests across Lean epochs are isolated and cancellable with deterministic results.\n- [ ] Every proof receipt carries theorem and axiom manifests with zero unapproved axioms.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nG6's doctrine — agent proof repair accepted ONLY by kernel — needs an isolated, cancellable service boundary; failure consequence per the matrix was \"no remote proof lane\"."}	blake3:aasJI9TbIh2gDArXvz8lko2tC7c_O-CDgVm6BRutj3A
1785294221404806	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypQI		item.update	bn-3ix	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nPhase E's opening PR (plan §21.1): Continuum Forge v0 — synthesis under verification, finite and honest. Closes re-homed G0-DX-07 (Forge non-vacuity; artifact shape from the Phase A spike, engine evidence here per plan §22). START_HERE PR 29. Forge may not be imported by the verifier (dependency-island rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTyped holes; finite grammar enumeration; exact counterexample feedback; safety plus progress/non-vacuity objectives; candidate archive; independent candidate verification (candidates are proposals — the ordinary evidence path grades them, Forge grades nothing itself).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The acknowledgement-guard task synthesizes `synced`, rejects never-ack/`false` (vacuous) candidates, and independently verifies the result (plan §25's from-scratch demonstration: ack_guard = synced).\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nNon-vacuity is Forge's soul: without a progress objective, synthesis returns the guard that never acknowledges. The spike proved the objective shape; this makes it an engine."}	blake3:a0XSdhNM3Rr8L-IAUjSbFpZFmP8mMOpIDM18A_hZsGI
