1785346237518954	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEuvAc		item.create	bn-3cgt	{"description":"# Authoritative requirement\n`G0-DX-02` — Can Continuum detect formal reward hacking?\nSource: `notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md:10`.\n\n# Experiment\npatches that weaken property, strengthen assumptions, reduce bounds, hide observer events, remove faults\n\n# Pass condition\nall classified as intent changes; ordinary code guard repair is not\n\n# Failure consequence\nblock autonomous repair\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nExecute the falsification experiment against the production implementation, including adversarial controls and the named baseline. A finite artifact-shape spike is not sufficient evidence.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone.","kind":"task","labels":["plan-key:experiment-g0-dx-02","g0","quality","req:g0-dx-02","req:phase-a","req:pr-12"],"parent":"bn-1r9","size":"m","title":"G0-DX-02 falsification — Can Continuum detect formal reward hacking?"}	blake3:9MVxsgsqktHZoneM_Xspacsx729l3t0JKbAq-KJWpKc
