1785346241538252	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEuzwg		item.create	bn-1s21	{"description":"# Authoritative requirement\n`T15` — Common-mode compiler bug\nSource: `notes/plan/docs/09_THREAT_MODEL.md:227`.\n\n# Required controls\n- foreign oracle corpus\n- independent kernel implementation path\n- potentially compile kernel with diverse toolchain\n- mechanized reference\n- serialization-level conformance vectors.\n- append-only\n- monotonic local sequence number\n- causal predecessor IDs\n- clock uncertainty\n- explicit loss marker\n- schema digest\n- implementation build digest\n- field redaction map\n- integrity chain.\n- bounded integer widths or arbitrary precision with allocation limits\n- canonical representation rejection\n- duplicate ID rejection\n- cycle/conflict validation\n- no path/URL dereference\n- no executable payload\n- stable error codes\n- checker never panics on input.\n- cargo-fuzz targets for every decoder\n- property tests for canonical encodings\n- malicious graph/certificate generator\n- pack honesty mutants\n- trace loss/reordering/tampering\n- solver proof corruption\n- replay sandbox escape tests\n- supply-chain bill of materials.\n- Minting. Identities are minted through audited daemon operations. The solo-developer default is a local keypair minted on first use and recorded in the audit log.\n- Trust-root distribution. Organizational deployments pin an allowed-signers set distributed inside the intent bundle (plan §4.2.1).\n- Rotation and revocation. Both are audited daemon operations.\n- Loss recovery. A lost key is not recovered; recovery re-mints under a new identity with an audit-linked supersession record.\n- Verification failure. A signature that cannot be verified downgrades the artifact to typed unverified provenance rather than failing open — except the plan §4.2.1 CI acceptance check, which fails closed by policy.\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nImplement every listed control at the actual trust boundary, retain a hostile fixture or exploit mutant, and prove assurance can only stay equal or weaken on failure.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone.","kind":"task","labels":["plan-key:threat-t15","quality","req:phase-d","req:t15","threat"],"parent":"bn-1i5n","size":"s","title":"T15 — Common-mode compiler bug"}	blake3:2n14IGJ8_VOThmXIejyTUaQnVjJkQ8Jm5SbI5HkLJ1E
1785346241566911	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEu0Ag		item.create	bn-34a8	{"description":"Manual decision ledger for docs/08 risks and plan §24 kill criteria. Evidence tasks may execute autonomously; accepting a kill/defer/narrow decision remains privileged.","kind":"goal","labels":["plan-key:risk-and-kill","goal:manual","governance","req:program","risk"],"parent":"bn-3dl","size":"l","title":"Risk retirement, kill-signal assays, and scope decisions"}	blake3:eF6BnThZY3C012nb59dXB9w1Ogc0v_b7rXbv9xjSg84
