1785348475944769	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxQI		item.link	bn-5kmuf	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-19p"}	blake3:BuLTqjhpWFNChPJXz3jcnzLt_MRpeBl3GtA2z0UD-rA
1785348476015150	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxgI		item.create	bn-4ykgg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPR 21 (START_HERE:375) requires generating semantic neighbors around the causal core; the graph carried only the G0-DX-06 falsification spike and the exit-evidence Bone.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nGenerate neighbors by perturbing the PR 18 causal core along semantic dimensions — interleaving, timing, fault placement, value domain — rather than by mutating the concrete trace. Neighbors are derived from the CIR so they remain well-typed against the intent. Record the generation strategy list and per-receipt coverage.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Neighbors are semantically valid against the Intent Contract, not arbitrary trace edits.\n- [ ] Generation is deterministic and reproducible from the core plus a recorded seed.\n- [ ] The strategy list and its coverage are disclosed per receipt, so a repair receipt states which neighborhood it survived.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe register fallback if neighborhood adequacy cannot ratify is exactly 'fixed strategy-list neighborhood with per-receipt coverage disclosure and NO adequacy claim'. Building disclosure in from the start means the fallback is a labeling change, not a rewrite.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","repair","req:phase-b","req:pr-21"],"parent":"bn-2gm","size":"m","title":"Semantic neighbor generation around the causal core"}	blake3:Bq9nbqtzxAkqihj3BvdoRYmCyHZnfxxQeae4az8c108
