1785348476115801	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyygI		item.create	bn-84rea	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe second half of PR 21 (START_HERE:375): run known property and model mutants against a candidate repair and grade the result inside the declared bounded envelope.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nMaintain a mutant corpus of property weakenings and model changes classified per docs/50. Run each candidate repair against neighbors and mutants; grade pass/fail strictly inside the bounded envelope so a repair can never be credited beyond what was actually explored. Wire the hidden-variant catch rate into the research/33 ratification evidence.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A hard-coded exact-trace repair fails the campaign; the semantic guard repair passes.\n- [ ] Grading never reports a result outside the declared envelope bounds (INV-007).\n- [ ] Hidden-variant catch rate is recorded as evidence for the neighborhood-adequacy register row (Phase B deadline).\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThis is what makes promotion mean something: without a mutation challenge, 'the exact replay passes' is gameable by memorizing the trace.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","repair","req:phase-b","req:pr-21"],"parent":"bn-2gm","size":"m","title":"Property/model mutation challenge and bounded-envelope grading"}	blake3:GdJSDVNr_y74FX-i6vqlOuxrM7T3eLrGZcrecFj_W0Y
