1785348476218066	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzgI		item.create	bn-3c78s	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPR 24 (START_HERE:413) requires randomly and deterministically comparing incremental against clean-build results at a sampled rate derived from §8.6's confidence target. The graph carried only the G0-DX-05 spike and the exit-evidence Bone.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nImplement the audit as a scheduled differential: sample queries at the §8.6-derived rate, recompute them clean, and compare against the incremental result. Sampling is seeded and reproducible so an audit run can be replayed exactly. Mismatches are recorded as first-class evidence nodes, not log lines.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The sampling rate is derived from §8.6's confidence target and the derivation is recorded, not hard-coded.\n- [ ] An audit run replays exactly from its seed (INV-006).\n- [ ] Every mismatch becomes an evidence-graph node with provenance to both computations.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe audit is the empirical backstop for every reuse claim in the incremental engine. If it is not reproducible, a mismatch cannot be investigated and the reuse claim cannot be defended.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","incremental","req:phase-c","req:pr-24"],"parent":"bn-1ay","size":"m","title":"Deterministic sampled incremental-vs-clean differential audit"}	blake3:IUnCnOkriz8j_tYCSRZNrxaeO_IPgZto82vMGN6YgOU
