1785348476218224	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0AI		item.link	bn-3p790	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3c78s"}	blake3:2zdTEmHhd1CT9sWTcVR0nkCOfZbCOLno1QlKeycGXto
1785348476246407	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0QI		item.link	bn-3c78s	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3zt"}	blake3:SWT6Tnn9VdVkLcJ8afYQqR0A6OzACRP2pqKmnQaJ4RI
1785348476314596	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0gI		item.create	bn-r4x4v	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPR 24's exit criterion — an intentionally broken dependency edge is caught and quarantined (START_HERE:413) — needs both a minimizer and the RFC 0030 auditability-class quarantine absorbed from plan §9.5.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nOn mismatch, minimize to the smallest dependency edge set that reproduces the divergence, then quarantine the affected auditability class so results in that class fall back to clean computation until the edge is fixed. Quarantine is class-scoped, not global, so one bad edge does not disable all reuse.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An intentionally broken dependency edge is caught, minimized to that edge, and quarantined.\n- [ ] Quarantine is scoped to the RFC 0030 auditability class; unaffected classes keep reusing.\n- [ ] Quarantined classes are visible in the assurance envelope — reuse that is currently untrusted is never reported as trusted.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe research/27 kill signal is that dependency capture cannot be trusted below file/module granularity. Class-scoped quarantine is what makes the fallback to module-granularity invalidation a graceful degradation rather than a cliff.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","incremental","req:phase-c","req:pr-24"],"parent":"bn-1ay","size":"m","title":"Invalidation-mismatch minimization and class-scoped quarantine"}	blake3:FYf_LfiY5PKKy6kXzepNe8AScW9a95B-pNpT1lhUF-M
