1785348476450223	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2QI		item.link	bn-sph8k	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3zt"}	blake3:H0pfstcoqMnUcQMKDbJzCS6PyTrcJ5Tq37O8FsaYHJA
1785348476524267	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2gI		item.create	bn-2i95u	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe diagnostic and navigation half of PR 25 (START_HERE:421), over the overlay snapshot model.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nPublish CML and source diagnostics from check results with source locations resolved through the PR 17 concrete/abstract correspondence. Semantic hover shows the elaborated meaning of the construct under the cursor; go-to correspondence jumps between model and implementation sites through the correspondence relation, not through name matching.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Diagnostics carry evidence handles so a squiggle is traceable to the artifact that produced it.\n- [ ] Hover reports the elaborated semantic meaning, not a syntactic restatement.\n- [ ] Go-to correspondence resolves through the correspondence relation; a deliberately name-mismatched pair still resolves correctly.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThis is where the G5 edit/check/explain loop is actually lived. Routing navigation through correspondence rather than names is what keeps the model and the code from drifting apart silently.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:phase-c","req:pr-25","ux"],"parent":"bn-2yb","size":"m","title":"CML/source diagnostics, semantic hover, and go-to correspondence"}	blake3:kesgwUhRyvwTeqIYlA5XHHQpGspoRdnPQC0H5wsSy0A
