1785348476552703	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3QI		item.link	bn-2i95u	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3zt"}	blake3:3PFHPuH-Cww53DR9jmWZSjL3KNsXe699Y22TIeuC6EQ
1785348476624696	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3gI		item.create	bn-ppr6w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe authoring-time half of PR 25 (START_HERE:421): code lenses and intent-change preview over snapshots.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nSurface code lenses for check/explain/debug actions at model and correspondence sites. Intent-change preview runs the PR 12 semantic diff against the overlay snapshot and shows, before save, whether an edit is a privileged intent change — the G3 classification surfaced at authoring time rather than at promotion time.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An edit that weakens a property is shown as a privileged intent change in the editor before it is saved.\n- [ ] Preview uses the same PR 12 diff engine as promotion — there is no second, weaker classifier.\n- [ ] Lenses degrade to text-only affordances with color and graphs disabled (feeds G8-06).\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSurfacing G3 semantics at authoring time is the difference between a guard rail and a gate that people learn to route around.\n","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:phase-c","req:pr-25","ux"],"parent":"bn-2yb","size":"m","title":"Code lenses and intent-change preview at authoring time"}	blake3:Rn0mGq1eicHnIR0Mw64PZet8zqccZdKOUzZXdHJNg5k
