1785348476832817	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5gI		item.create	bn-2zzs0	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe second half of PR 26 (START_HERE:439): expose the causal operations that have no DAP equivalent as custom requests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nExpose branch (fork the failure at a causal position), why-enabled, and why-blocked as DAP custom requests with documented schemas. A client that does not understand the custom requests still gets a working standard debugging experience — the causal operations are additive, never load-bearing for basic inspection.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A VS Code-compatible client can branch the replicated-register failure and inspect both successors.\n- [ ] Custom request schemas are published and versioned alongside the adapter.\n- [ ] A client that ignores the custom requests still completes standard inspection.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBranching and why-not questions are the operations that make this a verification debugger rather than a trace viewer; graceful degradation keeps the adapter usable across the editor ecosystem.\n","kind":"task","labels":["debugger","implementation","req:phase-c","req:pr-26"],"parent":"bn-21g","size":"m","title":"DAP custom requests for causal operations (branch, why-enabled/blocked)"}	blake3:qV-LqHfRONbYuohOnTfbO69nTGCwABLRm21W0nqALMI
