1785348477256707	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9gI		item.create	bn-317c2	{"description":"# Context & Background\n`PR-15B-IMPL-03` is a sequencing obligation, not a code change, and was bundled onto the formatter Bone. It gates the PHASE-C-DEL-07 declaration.\nSource: `notes/plan/notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md:309`.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTreat CML syntax stability as a gated declaration: it may not be announced until both the deterministic formatter and the migration tool are shipped and green on the replicated-register model and the Wave 0 CML ports. Record the declaration and its evidence in the Phase C exit package.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The syntax-stability declaration is blocked in CI until formatter and migration tool are both shipped and green.\n- [ ] The declaration cites the artifact evidence for both tools.\n- [ ] PHASE-C-DEL-07 is closed by this declaration, not by the formatter alone.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nDeclaring stability without a migration path strands every existing model at the first syntax revision — the classic way a young language loses its early adopters.\n","kind":"task","labels":["cml","implementation","req:phase-c","req:phase-c-del-07","req:pr-15b","req:pr-15b-impl-03"],"parent":"bn-380","size":"s","title":"PR-15B / IMPL-03 — formatter and migration tool ship before CML syntax stability is declared"}	blake3:QXLTvIziwQ-XRkVcaR7fj4qybtujGb_i28HoSHUgeeg
