1785348477359877	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-gI		item.create	bn-u4b3q	{"description":"# Context & Background\n`PR-26A-IMPL-02` was bundled onto the journaling Bone (bn-2182). The opaque-effect inventory is the half of the read-only tokio lane that makes its honesty claim, and it needs its own evidence-owning work item.\nSource: `notes/plan/notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md:445`.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nEnumerate, for an unmodified tokio program, everything the observation lane cannot observe — unobserved syscalls, foreign FFI, untracked time sources, unmonitored channels — and emit it as a structured inventory attached to the run. The inventory is what caps the assurance envelope at `Observed` with every claim dimension `Unsupported`.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every run emits an opaque-effect inventory; a run with no inventory is rejected, not treated as fully observed.\n- [ ] The inventory is structured and machine-readable, and is referenced by the assurance envelope (INV-007).\n- [ ] A program with a deliberately unobservable effect shows that effect in the inventory rather than silently omitting it.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThis lane's entire integrity rests on stating what it did not see. Without an inventory, 'observed' quietly reads as 'complete', which is exactly the T05 threat (incomplete production observation presented as validity).\n","kind":"task","labels":["adapter","implementation","req:phase-c","req:pr-26a","req:pr-26a-impl-02"],"parent":"bn-3b0","size":"m","title":"PR-26A / IMPL-02 — opaque-effect inventory for everything not observable"}	blake3:dTS-Rcqzt3uTRAEVToOQUD0PeQbxGkNDplg69lO4v9Y
