1785348477836442	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiwM		item.create	bn-30fmi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPhase E ships the Forge (synthesis) and the end-to-end agent benchmark. Synthesis output and explanation surfaces are exactly where over-claiming is easiest, and the G8 study grades against the docs/48 preregistration — so the documented surface must match what actually ships before the study runs.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nAs PR 29 and PR 30 land, reconcile the Forge synthesis contracts (non-vacuity, bounded envelope, materialization to the asupersync skeleton), the benchmark harness protocol, and the docs/48 explanation surface against the implementation. Any change to an explanation surface the preregistration measures is reconciled before the Phase F study runs, or explicitly recorded as a deviation.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Forge synthesis and materialization contracts describe the shipped behavior as built at the exit gate.\n- [ ] The benchmark harness protocol is documented well enough for an independent party to reproduce a run.\n- [ ] Explanation-surface changes are reconciled against docs/48 before the G8 study, or recorded as preregistration deviations.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nG8 is graded only against fixed preregistered thresholds. If the explanation surface drifts from what was preregistered without that drift being recorded, the study result is not interpretable.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","governance","quality","req:phase-e"],"parent":"bn-4rm","size":"m","title":"Normative documentation reconciliation — Phase E (Forge contracts, docs/48 explanation surface)"}	blake3:5xlVBmKtxvfNtx4hnHaMgpJmWa38_AcXp5YSEUPOq_4
