1785350483595987	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEurDQ		item.create	bn-3dg5b	{"description":"# Authoritative requirement\n`FR-02` — Exploration reduction (§9, INV-013)\nSource: `notes/plan/plan.md:2565`.\n\n# Promotion threshold / kill\nresearch/01 (stated there as a kill): at least an order-of-magnitude reduction on a non-artificial subset without a serious regression on dependent workloads (the \"explored classes\" denominator is a proposed ratification, to be fixed in research/01 before this row leaves draft); observer-indexed (docs/31): median ≥5× on the observer-sensitive class, *checker* overhead <20% (distinct from the certificate-overhead row), zero mutation loss; kill (docs/31, research/13): witness cost dominates, or observer/property changes invalidate cached independence so often that reuse never pays for its witness cost — draft\n\n# Fallback\nconservative unreduced exploration\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nDuring the phase before Phase C, fix the lane's numeric threshold and denominator, quote it verbatim in the authoritative register with matching quote-id markers, validate the fallback, and leave the consumer blocked if ratification fails.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone.","kind":"task","labels":["plan-key:frontier-fr-02","phase-c","req:fr-02","req:phase-c","research"],"parent":"bn-2z3","size":"s","title":"Ratify exploration-reduction thresholds and denominator"}	blake3:BL-JUHvZcCEYgbZ9QooiIrDigIoxP2d-sIKKSY4Vfro
