1785350483727771	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEusDQ		item.create	bn-187wu	{"description":"# Authoritative requirement\n`FR-10` — Bidirectional lenses (§16)\nSource: `notes/plan/plan.md:2573`.\n\n# Promotion threshold / kill\nambiguity rate := fraction of abstract edits on the drift corpus yielding multiple or no concrete candidates (metric per research/31; the drift corpus is the lane deliverable; the numeric target is fixed in the note at ratification and quoted here) — draft; kill if most real mappings are too ambiguous, or users mistake candidate synchronization for verified preservation (measured under the G8 instruments)\n\n# Fallback\nget-only projection + drift detection\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nDuring the phase before Phase D, fix the lane's numeric threshold and denominator, quote it verbatim in the authoritative register with matching quote-id markers, validate the fallback, and leave the consumer blocked if ratification fails.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone.","kind":"task","labels":["plan-key:frontier-fr-10","phase-d","req:fr-10","req:phase-d","research"],"parent":"bn-2z3","size":"s","title":"Ratify bidirectional-lens ambiguity threshold and fallback"}	blake3:0ibLMOlAnCrCgcHcO7WkY-2vUWkFeKJKaSfocIgpYrw
