1785350484089880	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEuvDQ		item.create	bn-2uh80	{"description":"# Scope\nMerge docs/31's remaining cubical-reduction, semiring, assumption-synthesis, and abstraction-discovery thresholds into plan §24.5 so the program has one lane authority; reconcile disagreements in the source notes.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each residual threshold has one register row, baseline, promotion/kill criterion, fallback, and source citation.\n- [ ] Draft qualitative criteria stay visibly draft until quantified.\n- [ ] Register quote-identity and dossier validation pass.","kind":"task","labels":["plan-key:frontier-docs31-residuals","docs","governance","req:program","research"],"parent":"bn-2z3","size":"m","title":"Merge residual docs/31 thresholds into the authoritative frontier register"}	blake3:mEWsmbIu_3zZCec8-3WXTY2eiLIH-aV5Oa9bOJuFjeY
1785356663672972	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykgM		item.create	bn-3596f	{"description":"# Context\nAudit the generated Revision 3 Bones graph against the implementation sequence and Edict grooming rules. Repair false-ready work, preserve parallelism where prerequisites are real, and add risk routing for security-sensitive work.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Foundational scaffold/toolchain prerequisites block their consumers.\n- [ ] Cross-cutting invariant, threat, and kill assays do not dispatch before the implementation they exercise.\n- [ ] Security-sensitive bones carry risk:high; standard work remains default risk:medium.\n- [ ] Manual phase and exit gates remain goal:manual.\n- [ ] Traceability, graph integrity, dossier validation, and dispatch-frontier checks pass.","kind":"task","labels":["trace:meta","governance","risk:low"],"parent":"bn-3dl","size":"s","title":"Groom initial dispatch dependencies and risk routing"}	blake3:fBfD_bOMLmfNK_EukNWdbH1ToZMH05b2_rWmAshcN1M
