1785357190339168	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEuvjQ		item.update	bn-36eg	{"field":"description","value":"# Authoritative requirement\n`INV-018` — Corpus honesty\nSource: `notes/plan/plan.md:375`.\n\n# Contract\nCompatibility claims include unsupported features, configured bounds, expected verdict, state/trace parity, and proof status.\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nImplement the invariant as an executable architectural guard and permanent regression. Include a mutant that would violate it and prove the guard detects it.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone."}	blake3:EPeDDGUUd7GDQpWuwPlxXiE331ZT74WxywX_WhpRVwA
1785357190371867	continuum-planner	itc:v3:AWLJM-cnJyfyRAAAAAAAQdW-666_qAAAAAEuvzQ		item.update	bn-1s21	{"field":"description","value":"# Authoritative requirement\n`T15` — Common-mode compiler bug\nSource: `notes/plan/docs/09_THREAT_MODEL.md:227`.\n\n# Required controls\n- foreign oracle corpus\n- independent kernel implementation path\n- potentially compile kernel with diverse toolchain\n- mechanized reference\n- serialization-level conformance vectors.\n\n# Delivery and evidence\nImplement every listed control at the actual trust boundary, retain a hostile fixture or exploit mutant, and prove assurance can only stay equal or weaken on failure.\n\n- [ ] Implementation, policy, or experiment is complete at the cited scope.\n- [ ] Positive, negative, and boundary evidence is retained under stable artifact IDs.\n- [ ] Relevant clean, incremental, mutation, security, and documentation gates pass.\n- [ ] The requirement label remains attached to the evidence-owning Bone."}	blake3:F_vj-8MLWcfALr06ruQ-qwx2VhxCukSfs5WTjJjp0ow
