1785537617314582	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyygM		item.comment	bn-31mq	{"body":"Scaffolded the repo-root implementation Lean project at lean/ by copying the planning-dossier seed from notes/plan/lean/ verbatim (16 modules under Continuum/, root Continuum.lean, lakefile.toml), then adding lean/.gitignore (ignores /.lake/ and build/) and adapting lean/README.md's status section to reference this bone and the sibling PR-4A IMPL-02 (kernel-check, bn-fak5) and IMPL-03 (T0/T1 theorems) bones. notes/plan/lean/ is untouched (verified via diff -r, exits clean). lean-toolchain contains exactly 'leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1' (25 bytes, single trailing newline, verified byte-for-byte). lakefile.toml required no path adjustments for the new location (it has no location-relative references) and parses as valid TOML (checked with Python tomllib); package name 'continuum-metatheory' / lean_lib 'Continuum' preserved from the seed. Cross-checked that all 16 imports in Continuum.lean exactly match the 16 .lean files under Continuum/ (diff clean). Verification method: file-inspection only — elan/lake/lean are not installed on this machine (command -v elan/lake/lean all failed), so per task instructions no toolchain download or 'lake env lean --version' resolution was attempted and no lake build was run. Out of scope and untouched: kernel-checking/building the seed modules (bn-fak5), T0/T1 theorems (IMPL-03), Justfile, crates/ and Cargo files."}	blake3:EQpYOGH9uY4RVHc58X60_0u-DsXpxQryxsbkejaLHAc
