1785538150150532	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1QM		item.comment	bn-147t	{"body":"IMPL-01 complete in .maw/workspaces/bn-147t (commit 776e886). Created the Cargo workspace (resolver 3, edition 2024, rust-version 1.85, workspace lint table with missing_docs=warn as the landing spot for IMPL-04's unsafe_code policy) with all 42 crates from plan §20 under crates/ — the list expanded exactly, continuum-effects-{network,storage,time,process} as four crates, no continuum-protocol crate (native protocol documented as living in continuumd). Every crate is a minimal Cargo.toml + src/lib.rs whose //! doc states its responsibility (with plan/PR citations) and its dependency-boundary contract. Only one dependency edge is declared: continuum-cml-elab -> continuum-cml-syntax (PR 15a states it outright); every other crate is dependency-free on purpose, since a wrong edge is debt. Boundaries are enforced by tools/check_crate_boundaries.py (stdlib-only Python over 'cargo metadata --no-deps'): rules members-match-plan-20, no-protocol-crate, certificate-checker-not-search, model-core-not-asupersync, kernel-is-synchronous, forge-not-imported-by-verifier, adapters-are-sinks — all transitive over normal+build deps, dev-deps reported but not enforced. It ships a --self-test that injects each forbidden edge (direct and via an innocent hop) into a synthetic graph and fails if any goes uncaught, so the check cannot pass vacuously; 'just boundaries' runs the self-test first. Verified negatively by injecting continuum-certificate -> continuum-engine-explicit: exit 1 with the named rule. Added a root Justfile: check = fmt-check + lint (clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings) + test + boundaries + dossier validator; plus fmt, build, traceability, and an honest install recipe that succeeds with a message (no crate declares a [[bin]] yet; continuumd/PR 5 and continuum-cli/PR 13 are the future binaries). .gitignore extended for /target and Python __pycache__. 'just check' passes end to end on rustc/cargo 1.97.0 stable, just 1.57.0: fmt clean, clippy clean, 84 test binaries ok (0 tests), boundaries pass, dossier validator status=pass program_status=ready. No Lean, epoch, enum, or build-determinism work touched."}	blake3:q7qyzL-N2oeCPLIRNRzkBxqtWBEwsWMLB0ecEWS0CcQ
