1785538865966094	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9QM		item.comment	bn-2oy	{"body":"Ratified the Workbench security (§18) row of plan §24.5. Gate marker quote-id=workbench-security-promotion-gate, identical in research/35 (new 'Lane status (plan §24.5)' section) and the register cell. Gate: autonomous promotion stays disabled until one red-team corpus run against the current build and dependency epoch clears every case; corpus floor is >=45 cases derived by counting existing structure, not invented -- 10 red-team classes of research/35 x 3 prohibited outcomes from its own kill criterion (unprivileged intent-status alteration, unprivileged evidence-status alteration, isolation escape) = 30, plus 1 case per each of docs/49's 7 intent-policy blocks, plus 1 escape attempt per each of docs/49's 8 worker-isolation controls. Pass bar: every case refused by a trusted authority check AND recorded in the append-only audit log (a silent block fails, per docs/49 prompt-injection boundary and plan §18.5), zero unprivileged intent/evidence status alterations, zero isolation escapes. Any later successful case re-locks autonomous promotion until the corpus, enlarged with that case and its regression test, clears again in full; staleness rule follows docs/49 supply chain (dependency epoch change invalidates evidence). Fallback unchanged: human-approved promotion only; no project kill for an individual vulnerability. Regenerated traceability (FR-20 active -> satisfied, expected). validate_dossier.py: status pass, register_rows rows=21 ratified_quotes_checked=4. Files: notes/plan/research/35-security-of-agentic-verification-workbenches.md, notes/plan/plan.md (row only), notes/plan/notes/PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json, notes/plan/notes/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md. Committed 40e42fe."}	blake3:B2ddsQFo6XcoMtrmsHXEsNngi0lb6Wmt8p4z1gPtQ1k
1785538877677062	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9gM		item.comment	bn-17cw	{"body":"Set [workspace.lints.rust] unsafe_code = \"forbid\" in root Cargo.toml (all 42 crates opt in via [lints] workspace = true; verified via grep, 168 = 42*4 workspace=true lines). No crate-level overrides added: checked plan.md §20 (only continuum-kernel-* gets an explicit no-unsafe rule), docs/03_ASSURANCE_AND_TCB.md, docs/12_GOVERNANCE_AND_ENGINEERING.md ('unsafe forbidden by default'), and ADR-0001 (asupersync) -- none of the Revision 3 dossier reserves unsafe for continuum-asupersync or continuum-effects-*. Only the superseded notes/plan/archive/plan-revision-2.md section 16.2 had a boundary-crate carve-out, not carried into Revision 3, so no exception was made. Negative-evidence probe: added 'fn _forbid_unsafe_probe() { unsafe {} }' to crates/continuum-value/src/lib.rs, ran cargo check -p continuum-value, got: error: usage of an `unsafe` block --> crates/continuum-value/src/lib.rs:25:5 | 25 | unsafe {} | ^^^^^^^^^ | = note: requested on the command line with -F unsafe-code; error: could not compile continuum-value (lib) due to 1 previous error. Probe fully reverted (git diff showed only Cargo.toml changed afterward; continuum-value re-checked clean). just check passed end to end: fmt-check, clippy -D warnings, cargo test --workspace (all 0-test placeholders green), check_crate_boundaries.py self-test+run (42/42 members, 0 violations), dossier validation (status pass). Committed as 4e70171 in .maw/workspaces/bn-17cw."}	blake3:vb3zjMrsXW-ziO_RwiDjDZIRAxSugbHpoRla_bv2_oo
