1785538938729041	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-AM		item.move	bn-17cw	{"state":"done"}	blake3:o0HQ1SAWLHXYhfp1FGWsUWIy2Smm9XrMOaWlyJtCzh4
1785538949852503	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-QM		item.comment	bn-2ba	{"body":"Ratified neighborhood adequacy (FR-05), lane opened. N = 20 hidden mutations per docs/50 attack class across all five classes (intent, instrumentation, evidence, overfitting, resource) => corpus >= 100 mutations; catch-rate target = >= 90 percent overall, one-sided 95 percent exact binomial lower bound above 80 percent, no single attack class below 75 percent; a catch counts only when property-directed neighboring exploration surfaces a neighbor on which the gaming patch fails and the receipt discloses it, on a family-level held-out split graded by the independent grader of research/33. Rationale: docs/50 names 25 techniques across 5 classes (largest class = 6), and 3 realizations per named technique (research/25 seed precedent) gives 18, rounded to a uniform per-class floor of 20; at 100 mutations a truly-80-percent neighborhood reaches 90/100 only ~0.6 percent of the time while a truly-95-percent one passes ~99 percent of the time, and Clopper-Pearson at 90/100 is 0.836 so the point target binds and the interval guard is satisfiable; 95 percent was rejected because discriminating it needs several hundred independently graded mutations, which is the grading-cost kill criterion. Kill clause (hidden variants too easy to leak or too hard to grade independently) and the fixed strategy-list fallback retained. Marker quote-id=neighborhood-adequacy-catch-rate identical in research/33 and plan.md 24.5. Regenerated traceability (FR-05 active -> satisfied, frontier satisfied 3 -> 4); validate_dossier.py status: pass, ratified_quotes_checked 4. Commit b0a174e."}	blake3:HtlqVhb9uevrjyb3YHzP8Sy9vv6snLWDAIJCpN2OQqA
1785539003083771	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-gM		item.move	bn-2ba	{"state":"done"}	blake3:W0TraCw2N5gnJLt9j0HwXlbMK9lfxpbfi2G04hUWw0k
1785539019443861	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-wM		item.comment	bn-1o2	{"body":"Ratified the multi-agent evidence-graph enforcement row (plan §24.5, FR-21). Marker quote-id=evidence-graph-enforcement now lives in notes/plan/research/08-agentic-verification.md under a new 'Lane status (plan §24.5)' section and is quoted verbatim in the register cell. Criteria: the four §11.7 properties (trusted-service-only promotion, per-claim linearized CAS with no lattice regression and no lost promotion, deterministic conflict materialization, idempotent retry) must hold with zero counterexamples under BOTH exhaustive exploration of a bounded write-protocol model at 3 concurrent writers over 2 claim identities AND an adversarial campaign against a persistent continuumd of >=1,000 seeded schedules per configuration over the docs/19 §7 determinism matrix (writer counts 1/2/8/32 on one claim identity, debug+release, process restarts), with typed StatusConflict on 100% of losing CAS, original node identity on 100% of replayed idempotency keys, exactly one Conflict node per contradictory pair whose content identity is byte-identical across schedules/seeds/worker counts/restarts, and per-claim promotion histories accepted by an independent linearizability checker against the §11.4 lattice; one violation in one trial fails the lane. Rationale: 2 writers is the spike's own configuration so 3 is the smallest count exposing non-pairwise races, 2 claim identities falsifies a global lock posing as per-claim ordering, the matrix numbers are docs/19 §7 verbatim, and the 1,000-schedule floor is the rule-of-three bound (<0.3% per-schedule violation rate at 95% confidence, ~5x tighter than the 1-in-64 sampled-audit default). Kill added: properties achievable only by serializing every writer behind one global lock, or nondeterministic conflict artifacts; fallback unchanged (single-writer graph, one integrator role). Lane cell now names research/08; RFC 0038 gained a one-line cross-reference. Traceability regenerated (FR-21 -> satisfied); validate_dossier.py status: pass, ratified_quotes_checked 5. Commit 5c4d013."}	blake3:B3Gi43aJ4ZvJLvf3XzOllReZ10y3aIMjAspT78EYqss
1785539054633893	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_AM		item.comment	bn-fak5	{"body":"lake build SUCCEEDS (19/19 jobs, zero errors, zero warnings) under leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1. Toolchain: elan was absent; installed user-locally via the official installer to ~/.elan and pulled v4.32.1 (lake env lean --version => 'Lean (version 4.32.1, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, commit f054605aea4b840552cca2e725580bffd1e1b704, Release)'). 'lake env lean Continuum.lean' also exits 0.\n\nOnly 2 of 16 modules were actually broken:\n- Continuum/Temporal.lean: trailing '/-- ... -/' doc comment attached to no declaration => parse error at 'end'. Converted to '/-! ... -/' section comment; text byte-identical.\n- Continuum/Examples/DieHard.lean: 'List.get?' no longer exists in Lean core, and 'Some' (capitalized) was being absorbed by autoImplicit. Rewrote the statement as 'solution[6]? = some <...>'; same proposition, still proved by 'decide'.\n\nTwo further one-line proof-term changes (build was already green, these cleared linter.unnecessarySimpa warnings AND removed axiom deps):\n- Continuum/Refinement.lean:62 'simpa [hlower]' -> 'exact congrArg toAbstract hlower'\n- Continuum/Interaction/Incremental.lean:14 'simpa [witness.inputsEqual]' -> 'exact congrArg query witness.inputsEqual'\n\nAlso added lean/lake-manifest.json (no deps) for reproducible builds and updated lean/README.md status from 'source-level seed' to 'kernel-checked'.\n\nSORRY/AXIOM INVENTORY: 0 'sorry', 0 'admit', 0 'axiom' declarations across all 16 modules. No theorem statement was altered, deleted, or downgraded to sorry. No set_option, partial, unsafe, native_decide, or implemented_by anywhere. grep -rn 'sorry|axiom' Continuum/ returns 3 lines, all in ProofReceipt.lean and all substring hits on the DATA field 'axioms : List String' and its doc comment - not Lean axiom commands.\n\n#print axioms for all 24 public theorems: 22 depend on NO axioms. The 2 exceptions depend on propext alone: Continuum.cancel_step_decreases_rank (simp) and Continuum.Examples.DieHard.solution_ends_with_four_gallons (decide). Notably the three T0/T1-relevant theorems are already fully axiom-free: TransitionSystem.reachable_satisfies, StutteringSimulation.maps_reachable, ClosureCertificate.provesSafety.\n\nNothing left broken; nothing excluded. Committed as ed23df8. NOT DONE (follow-up bone): wiring 'lake build' into 'just check' - the Justfile is untouched, so CI does not yet run this."}	blake3:5VUHEOOo4wtR7sUxN9wV0bL2Tb0AR6udwgLLQgWJKJc
