1785539347724226	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEygwQ		item.comment	bn-3oehf	{"body":"PR-1 / IMPL-02 landed in crates/continuum-value/src/epoch.rs (commit b05432d in .maw/workspaces/bn-3oehf).\n\nCrate: continuum-value. Plan §4.6 states 'Epochs are content identities' and docs/33 'Trust boundary' puts content identity inside the smallest trust base — which is this crate's declared responsibility (plan §4.4, ADR-0013). It is also the workspace's only declared leaf crate, so kernel, certificate, evidence, corpus, proof-client and continuumd can share one epoch vocabulary without new edges into the certificate/kernel closure. Zero dependency edges added; Cargo.lock untouched; stdlib only.\n\nTypes: EpochKind (all six, PR-1 order); EpochIdentity + EpochIdentityError (canonical printable-ASCII token, exact equality, no Ord — plan §4.6 identities have no computable successor); SemanticEpoch / IntentEpoch / EvidenceEpoch / ProofEpoch / CorpusEpoch as distinct newtypes (RFC 0026 'MUST NOT be conflated' enforced by the type system); ProtocolEpoch (major.minor, Ord, Display/FromStr round-trip per RFC 0026 '3.0', negotiate() = highest common version else None -> ProtocolVersionUnsupported) with ProtocolRange and ProtocolWindow (majors N and N-1); Compatibility (Preserved|Revalidate|Incompatible, plan §4.6) and EpochAdvance (rejects a no-op advance — advancing always yields a new identity); EpochBinding/EpochEntry/EpochSet, where entries() always returns all six kinds and unpinned ones read Unpinned rather than being omitted (seed of the PR-1 exit: 'names every epoch and no misleading success flag' — no success flag exists, only unpinned_kinds()); EpochSet::first_mismatch for continuation resume (plan §9.6, RFC 0026 ContinuationEpochMismatch).\n\nTests: 30 unit tests in crates/continuum-value/src/epoch.rs, incl. epoch_kind_names_every_epoch_pr_1_lists and an_unpinned_set_still_names_every_epoch.\n\njust check: fmt-check, lint (clippy -D warnings), test (30 pass), boundaries (status pass, 0 violations) all green. The dossier step fails on 'PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md is stale' — pre-existing and unrelated: reproduced on a pristine tree with my two files removed; the diff is only the frontier row (13->12 mapped, 5->6) from shared bones-state drift by a sibling agent. notes/ and .bones/ untouched."}	blake3:IiCPVS_0I0QjmMLv-ZfetjwtDjzUQ0QiU8Y-uts3dO0
