1785540249590535	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykwQ		item.comment	bn-2es0	{"body":"PR-1 / IMPL-03 implemented in crates/continuum-value/src/assurance.rs (leaf crate, same pattern as src/epoch.rs; plan §20 names no assurance crate and RFC 0026 requires the envelope on every semantic verdict, so the vocabulary sits where no consumer needs a new dependency edge).\n\nEnums: AssuranceLevel (RFC 0031 total order observed<sampled<bounded<validated<proved, the only Ord here) + AssuranceRequirement/AssuranceChange (no-downgrade classification, fail-closed on mixed changes); ValidationBasis (checked-certificate/trusted-solver, plan §11.4); EvidenceClass (RFC 0010's 13 classes, deliberately unordered); docs/03 §3 claim dimensions SemanticCoverage/ExplorationClass/ProofClass/ImplementationLinkage (product lattice, no Ord; ObservationCoverage omitted — docs/03 tabulates no levels for it); InconclusiveReason (INV-008's six: Unsupported, ResourceExhausted, EngineError, InsufficientTelemetry, AbstractionAmbiguity, IncompleteProofSearch — closed set, no catch-all); AssuranceDimension + AssuranceEnvelope (B11's nine dimensions, each naming a producing engine or a typed UnsupportedReason, never omitted, no success flag).\n\nSeams left for IMPL-06: the §11.4 status lattice and the established/refuted/inconclusive verdict are not defined here; the lattice's Inconclusive should carry InconclusiveReason and its Validated should carry ValidationBasis. continuum-evidence untouched, src/epoch.rs untouched.\n\n29 new tests (59 in crate). just check passes end to end: fmt-check, clippy -D warnings, cargo test --workspace, boundaries (42/42 crates, 0 violations), dossier validator status=pass. Commit 50e0aaf."}	blake3:924S1aAwSVI8HNAvibe5lEDg1Kph1_G_sCd5WKZIfNc
