1785540340315489	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymQQ		item.comment	bn-1lz	{"body":"SD-07 paid. intent-contract.schema.json now carries a structured property AST: claims[].expression and assumptions[].expression are $defs/property_expression objects ({ast, fragment?, normal_form?, source?}), and fairness[].condition is a temporal-operator-free state_formula (structurally enforced via a recursive temporal_free $def). Formula kinds: boolean, predicate (state atom), action (occurs|enabled), compare (eq/ne/lt/le/gt/ge/member/subset), not, and/or (n-ary, minItems 2), implies, iff, always/eventually, leads_to, forall/exists; term kinds: var, literal, constant, state, apply. 'next' is deliberately absent (LTL without next, RFC 0015 stuttering invariance); recurrence/persistence are spelled always(eventually)/eventually(always). Normalization spec: RFC 0037 new section 'Property AST and canonical normal form (CPNF-1)' — rules N1 derived-operator elimination, N2 negation-normal form, N3 associativity flattening, N4 commutative ordering + idempotence, N5 de Bruijn-level binder alpha-renaming, N6 comparison canonicalization, N7 boolean/temporal simplification (one-sided quantifier collapse), N8 canonical byte-deterministic encoding, N9 idempotence/determinism; plus soundness statements S1-S3 (equal normal forms => unchanged and nothing weaker; CPNF-1 sound but incomplete so unequal forms carry no direction; directional relations still need the fragment's decision procedure). Migration: retired bare string is rejected by the schema, its text survives in display-only 'source' which never contributes to in_* identity; unparseable strings fail closed; migration changes in_* identity and requires re-acceptance (SD-08 cross-schema versioning explicitly left untouched). Cross-refs added to RFC 0031 (property + assumptions/fairness bullets now read over CPNF-1) and docs/40 (new 'Property normalization' subsection). Example updated: schemas/examples/intent-contract.example.json — AckImpliesDurable becomes always(forall e in Events. acknowledged(e) => durable(e)), A-storage becomes always(SyncCompleted occurs => stable_recovery), fairness condition becomes predicate node_running; semantically identical. RFC 0026 untouched; only the SD-07 ledger line changed in plan.md §25 (now 'SD-07 (paid, PR 0)'). Traceability regenerated. validate_dossier.py: \"status\": \"pass\", spec_debt open = SD-01, SD-08, SD-09, SD-10; paid includes SD-07."}	blake3:8SzZ95QFqAcbPE5EI3TZlnhcbsTZpdWvUGbveVaOkFU
1785540390175171	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymgQ		item.comment	bn-2b8w	{"body":"PR-1 / IMPL-05 implemented in .maw/workspaces/bn-2b8w (commit 171b323).\n\n(a) Build-determinism POLICY. New rust-toolchain.toml pins channel=1.97.0 (exact patch, verified installed and active) with components=[clippy, rustfmt] — docs/12 §1 'Rust edition/toolchain pinned', plan §20 'kernel crates build reproducibly from pinned sources ... build digest and toolchain identity (INV-014) ... independently re-derivable', plan §4.2 (snapshots pin toolchain). Cargo.toml gains [profile.release] overflow-checks = true, justified by docs/19 §7's debug/release determinism-matrix dimension (silent wrapping in release vs panic in dev would make one scenario yield two semantic artifacts) plus docs/12 §11 'semantic digest nondeterminism'. debug-assertions deliberately left at default (a firing debug_assert is a detected divergence, not a misleading artifact). trim-paths deliberately NOT set: it is still unstable in Cargo 1.97.0 ('feature trim-paths ... not stabilized') — the omission is documented in-file and deferred to PR 9's kernel covenant rather than asserted with a nightly flag. Justfile lint/test/build now run --locked (docs/12 §5 'locked dependencies', plan §4.2 'dependency lockfiles'). README gains a short 'Deterministic builds' section. [workspace.lints] and the member list untouched.\n\n(b) Artifact-path CODE. New crates/continuum-workspace/src/artifact_path.rs (stdlib only, 19 plan §4.4 artifact classes in dossier order). Placed in continuum-workspace, not continuum-evidence: it is the top of the START_HERE dependency islands, so continuumd/task/evidence can share one store layout without importing each other; lib.rs edit is one 'pub mod artifact_path;' line plus a doc paragraph. API: ArtifactClass (ALL/token/prefix/is_content_addressed/from_token), ArtifactHandle (new + FromStr + Display, identity kept verbatim per ADR-0013), ArtifactPath::for_handle -> '<class>/<shard>/<identity>' (class first because plan §4.5 requires per-class storage attribution and per-class GC; SHARD_LEN=2 is the one non-dossier value and is a named public const), ArtifactPath::resolve(root), ArtifactLayout (BTreeMap-keyed, never a hash map — docs/19 §7 'different hash seeds'). Purity is the INV-005 point: no clock, counter, env, cwd, or entropy. cap_* is refused a content-derived path (plan §4.4: capability tokens 'are minted randomly and do confer authority' — filing a bearer secret under a path derived from itself would publish it into the directory namespace). Identity charset restricted to [A-Za-z0-9_-] per the normative schemas, which is also the path-traversal defense (docs/19 §9, docs/09).\n\nTests: 18 unit tests + 1 doctest, all passing. Coverage — plan §4.4 prefix list and order; class-token distinctness (the property that makes the first-underscore split unambiguous, incl. the in_/inb_ pair); wire-form round trip for all 19 classes; schema-pattern conformance; golden path literals (stability across process runs/rebuilds); purity (same handle via two construction routes); injectivity incl. case sensitivity; layout listing identical under forward/reversed/rotated/duplicated insertion order; sortedness; traversal rejection over 13 hostile identities ('..', 'a/b', 'a\\\\b', 'C:', UNC, NUL, newline, non-ASCII, RTL override); no relative/absolute segment in any derived path; resolve() stays under root; capability refusal on both for_handle and layout insert. Mutation-checked: flipping SHARD_LEN 2->3 fails golden_paths_are_stable and resolve_stays_under_the_root, so the goldens are not vacuous.\n\njust check: PASS end to end (fmt-check, clippy -D warnings --locked, cargo test --workspace --locked, crate boundaries + self-test, dossier validator status=pass / program_status=ready).\n\nNote for integrators: pinning 1.97.0 required installing the exact-patch toolchain (only '1.97' was present); it is installed locally now, but a fresh machine will fetch 1.97.0 on first cargo invocation. Also, --locked means a sibling adding a dependency must refresh and commit Cargo.lock or the gate fails — that is the intended friction."}	blake3:EqLCIqQlT23Ckhe1ZH4q8aMnaxk4-nD6VoItb4edqJs
