1785540534613245	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyngQ		item.comment	bn-11se	{"body":"PR-1 / IMPL-06 implemented in crates/continuum-evidence/src/claim_status.rs (new module, stdlib only, no new dependency edges; lib.rs exports it and records the placement rationale). Status set = the nine of plan §11.4 / RFC 0038 / evidence-graph-node.schema.json, tokens byte-identical to the schema enum; no 'draft', and 'conflict' is a node kind (§11.2), never a status. Order derived from an explicit, per-row cited cover table (ClaimStatus::COVERS): proposed ⋖ inconclusive ⋖ observed ⋖ sampled ⋖ bounded ⋖ validated ⋖ proved ⋖ refuted ⋖ superseded — docs/44's authority table fixes ⊥/⊤ and puts refuted above the assurance band, RFC 0031's normative 'observed < sampled < bounded < validated < proved' fixes the band, plan §11.4 'budget exhaustion is never a verdict' + INV-009 put inconclusive below it. The covers form a chain today; the module documents at length why (a partial order cannot make sampled→bounded a promotion while bounded→sampled is plan §5.1's downgrade, since incomparability is symmetric) and why docs/33 / RFC 0010's 'not totally ordered' is preserved in the assurance envelope (docs/03 product lattice), with order_is_a_chain as the tripwire if PR 0 amends the order. Regression predicate: StatusTransition::{Reassertion, Promotion, Regression}; a regression is exactly a lowering, permitted = to ≥ from (reflexive, so an idempotent replay is accepted per §11.7). Also ships the pure compare_and_set decision (typed StatusConflict of plan §10.3 for a lost CAS, LatticeRegression for a downgrade) and verify_promotion_history, the acceptance predicate the §24.5 / research-08 linearizability checker checks candidate orders against. 39 unit tests + 1 doctest, exhaustive over the 9-element set: reflexivity/antisymmetry/transitivity/chain, covers are strict Hasse edges and generate the order, join/meet are lub/glb with idempotence, commutativity, associativity, absorption and unit laws, all 81 ordered pairs classified, every docs/44-authorized transition permitted, plan §5.1 downgrades and superseded-reopening rejected, CAS and history-checker cases. Seam for IMPL-03 left documented and dependency-free: ClaimStatus::schema_obligations reports the INV-008 reason / validation_basis / service_identity requirements without restating continuum-value's InconclusiveReason and ValidationBasis; wiring is the PR-1 exit's job. just check passes end to end (fmt, clippy -D warnings, workspace tests, boundaries, dossier; exit 0). Committed b924394."}	blake3:iM3F4d7k2XG8aoLCG2_d190WLwvmL0CJBYaVYq-ff2g
